                <pb facs="0563" n="491" xml:id="pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2489/66.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Squiers to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-07-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 22,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Squiers reports that the minister for foreign affairs has particularly
                    requested him to ask the department for a categorical reply to the proposal of
                    Panama for the settlement of the <hi rendition="#italic">Columbia</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Buffalo</hi> cases, as Panama desires to close the
                    matter.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
